WEBVTT

00:00:09.738 --> 00:00:12.908
(MUSIC AND SINGING CONTINUE)

00:00:17.955 --> 00:00:21.416
-Okay, that's everyone, Mr. Moon.
-Phew!

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.336
All right, call everyone back to stage,
Miss Crawly, and let's get...

00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:25.712
-(FEEDBACK)
-Ohh!

00:00:25.796 --> 00:00:28.757
Hello! Can I have everybody
back to stage, please?

00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:31.093
Everyone come back to stage for selection.

00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:32.928
Okay. Thank you, Miss Crawly.

00:00:33.011 --> 00:00:35.097
You're welcome, Mr. Moon.

00:00:44.147 --> 00:00:46.275
All right. Let's see, now.

00:00:46.358 --> 00:00:47.359
(ANIMALS GASP)

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:48.735
Hmm.

00:00:52.281 --> 00:00:57.327
I'll take...

00:00:57.411 --> 00:00:58.620
-You guys.
-(CHEERING)

00:00:59.288 --> 00:01:00.455
And which one of you is the girl?

00:01:00.539 --> 00:01:02.040
Ha-ha. Very funny.

00:01:02.124 --> 00:01:05.127
"Loud and horrible, but shows promise."

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.920
-Welcome to the show.
-(SCOFFS)

00:01:07.004 --> 00:01:08.505
Cool. I guess we could hang.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.132
No, no. I just want her, not you.

00:01:10.215 --> 00:01:11.216
-What?
-What?

00:01:11.383 --> 00:01:13.969
All right, the rest of the group acts,
thank you so much.

00:01:14.177 --> 00:01:15.262
(DISAPPOINTED SIGHS)

00:01:15.387 --> 00:01:16.513
Oh, don't feel bad, folks.

00:01:16.597 --> 00:01:19.641
There'll be a 10% discount
on tickets for everyone!

00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:20.809
Yeah, sure, thanks a lot.

00:01:21.393 --> 00:01:24.062
(SCOFFS) Let's get out of here, Ash.

00:01:24.688 --> 00:01:25.814
Ash?

00:01:25.898 --> 00:01:27.608
Uh, yeah.

00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:28.984
Yeah, let's go.

00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:31.528
Okay, soloists!

00:01:32.195 --> 00:01:36.533
Johnny, Mike, Pete, Richard, Daniel and Ray.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.245
Mike! Wowza!

00:01:40.329 --> 00:01:41.747
I've got to have you in my show.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.373
(CHUCKLING) Oh. If you insist.

00:01:43.457 --> 00:01:44.833
And I'll take Pete.

00:01:45.292 --> 00:01:46.501
Oh, yeah!

00:01:46.585 --> 00:01:47.961
And one more.

00:01:49.087 --> 00:01:50.380
-Let me see now.
-(FARTS)

00:01:50.464 --> 00:01:52.424
Oh, my gosh. I am so sorry.

00:01:52.758 --> 00:01:53.967
(FARTS)

00:01:54.092 --> 00:01:55.260
(GASPS) What is wrong with me?

00:01:55.594 --> 00:01:58.221
Whoo! Uh, thanks for coming, Richard.

00:01:58.722 --> 00:01:59.681
(SIGHS)

00:01:59.765 --> 00:02:01.141
-(GRUNTS)
-(RAY SCREAMS)

00:02:01.224 --> 00:02:02.935
Oh, my... Ray!

00:02:03.518 --> 00:02:04.686
-Are you all right?
-(GROANS)

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.772
Just hang in there, Ray. I got you.

00:02:06.855 --> 00:02:08.941
-(FARTING)
-Oh! Oh! Oops!

00:02:10.859 --> 00:02:13.320
Okay, then I'll take...

00:02:15.155 --> 00:02:16.156
Daniel.

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:17.240
-Thank you, Johnny.
-(DISAPPOINTED SIGHS)

00:02:17.324 --> 00:02:19.242
Daniel, can you hear me?

00:02:19.368 --> 00:02:20.786
You're in the show!

00:02:20.869 --> 00:02:22.162
What?

00:02:22.245 --> 00:02:23.705
Are you talking to me?

00:02:24.206 --> 00:02:25.666
-Yes.
-(FEEDBACK)

00:02:25.999 --> 00:02:29.086
I was saying that you are in...

00:02:29.419 --> 00:02:31.463
Oh, geez, this is gonna
drive me nuts. Johnny!

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:33.173
Get back here. You're in.

00:02:33.256 --> 00:02:35.884
-Thank you, Daniel. Goodbye!
-(ALL GASP)

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:36.969
Yes!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.304
Okay. That's everyone on my list.

00:02:39.721 --> 00:02:40.806
(DISAPPOINTED SIGHS)

00:02:40.889 --> 00:02:43.392
Um, wait a second. Rosita.

00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:44.893
Is Rosita still here?

00:02:44.977 --> 00:02:46.520
Yes! Yes, I'm here!

00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:49.106
Rosita, Rosita, Rosita. "Great set of pipes,

00:02:49.231 --> 00:02:50.774
"but boring to watch."

00:02:50.857 --> 00:02:53.026
(SIGHS) I knew it.

00:02:53.151 --> 00:02:54.695
So, what should I do?

00:02:54.778 --> 00:02:58.323
I could partner you up with Gunter.

00:02:58.407 --> 00:02:59.658
Gunter! Where are you?

00:03:00.283 --> 00:03:02.452
Ja! Ja! This is me.

00:03:04.579 --> 00:03:07.082
(LAUGHS) Ja!

00:03:07.207 --> 00:03:08.500
It's gonna spice things up on stage.

00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:10.961
Wait. You want us to sing together?

00:03:11.044 --> 00:03:13.380
Ja! The two of us together, you joking me?

00:03:13.463 --> 00:03:15.882
We're going to be spicy, no?
(LAUGHS EXCITEDLY)

00:03:17.009 --> 00:03:19.219
That koala's a fool, Sherry-Anne!

00:03:19.302 --> 00:03:21.221
You are gonna be a star one day!

00:03:21.304 --> 00:03:24.516
Auditions are over, pal.
Show's already been cast.

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:28.145
Okay. You are my chosen few.

00:03:28.228 --> 00:03:29.479
-Yes!
-(ALL EXCLAIM EXCITEDLY)

00:03:29.563 --> 00:03:33.900
This is it, folks!
A defining moment in all of our lives!

00:03:34.151 --> 00:03:35.152
Um, no...

00:03:35.277 --> 00:03:37.779
No, no, no. Not you guys.
I dismissed all of the group acts already.

00:03:37.863 --> 00:03:38.947
You can go home.

00:03:39.031 --> 00:03:41.324
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

00:03:41.408 --> 00:03:45.370
Look, I'm really sorry,
but all of the slots are filled.

00:03:45.454 --> 00:03:47.497
(CONTINUES SPEAKING JAPANESE)

00:03:47.581 --> 00:03:48.999
-(MUSIC PLAYING)
-No, no, listen!

00:03:49.082 --> 00:03:50.834
No in show.

00:03:50.917 --> 00:03:52.252
Goodbye-bye!

00:03:52.335 --> 00:03:53.336
-(MUSIC STOPS)
-Miss Crawly!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.380
-(GIGGLING)
-Come on, you guys! Out of here.

00:03:55.505 --> 00:03:57.132
Come on. Off the stage.

00:03:57.215 --> 00:03:58.717
Thank you so much.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.052
Hey, Moon. What's the story?

00:04:00.135 --> 00:04:01.636
Is the prize really inside this thing?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.014
The prize? Oh, sure. Yes, it's all in there.

00:04:04.389 --> 00:04:07.392
Open it, will ya?
I wanna see what $100,000 looks like.

00:04:07.476 --> 00:04:09.603
JOHNNY: Me, too!
ROSITA: Yeah, go on. Open it, Mr. Moon.

00:04:09.686 --> 00:04:10.812
Sure, I'll open it.

00:04:11.271 --> 00:04:13.315
Wait. What did you say?

00:04:13.398 --> 00:04:15.358
He said $100,000.

00:04:16.651 --> 00:04:17.944
A hundred... (YELPS)

00:04:18.612 --> 00:04:20.113
Uh... (NERVOUS CHUCKLE)

00:04:21.406 --> 00:04:23.075
I forgot my keys.

00:04:23.158 --> 00:04:24.409
Koala be right back.

00:04:26.161 --> 00:04:27.579
(CRYING)

00:04:27.662 --> 00:04:31.583
For the last time, Miss Crawly,
I'm not going to fire you!

00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:33.043
Now would you pull yourself together

00:04:33.126 --> 00:04:35.212
and please blow that nose of yours.

00:04:35.295 --> 00:04:36.254
(BLOWING NOSE)

00:04:36.338 --> 00:04:38.673
No, no, no. Not in here. Blow it outside.

00:04:38.757 --> 00:04:39.758
MISS CRAWLY: I'm sorry.
BUSTER: Thank you.

00:04:39.841 --> 00:04:42.094
Buster, what do you expect?
She's, like, 200 years old.

00:04:42.177 --> 00:04:45.555
Eddie, please. Look, if your folks could
just loan me the money until...

00:04:45.639 --> 00:04:49.059
$100,000? Buster, come on!

00:04:49.142 --> 00:04:50.519
(EXHALES) I got to think, I've got to think,

00:04:50.602 --> 00:04:51.770
I've got to think.

00:04:51.895 --> 00:04:56.233
Look, maybe it's time to stop thinking,
and it's time to just move on.

00:04:56.316 --> 00:04:59.903
I mean, this theater of yours, you could get
some decent money for it and...

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.863
I don't know,
maybe we could do something together.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.825
What? What, sit around playing video games?

00:05:04.908 --> 00:05:06.034
(EXCLAIMS)

00:05:06.201 --> 00:05:08.036
Do you know what that is?

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.121
Uh, it's a bucket?

00:05:09.204 --> 00:05:11.456
Yes, and do you know why I have this bucket?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.541
Because the roof is leaking?

00:05:12.624 --> 00:05:14.668
No, that's the bucket for the leak.

00:05:14.751 --> 00:05:17.712
I have this one
because it belonged to my father.

00:05:18.338 --> 00:05:19.589
Every day for 30 years,

00:05:19.673 --> 00:05:21.883
he worked his tail off washing cars

00:05:21.967 --> 00:05:23.844
just so I could buy this place.

00:05:24.886 --> 00:05:26.555
Every day, Eddie.

00:05:27.055 --> 00:05:28.765
Just for me. (SIGHS)

00:05:28.849 --> 00:05:31.810
Wow. Sounds like a great dad.

00:05:33.145 --> 00:05:34.146
(SIGHS)

00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:35.897
So how do you wanna handle this?

00:05:35.981 --> 00:05:37.357
(INTERCOM BEEPS)

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.612
MISS CRAWLY: Uh, Mr. Moon, I got Judith
from the bank holding on line two again.

00:05:44.948 --> 00:05:45.991
(SIGHS)

00:05:46.074 --> 00:05:47.534
Well, there's only one thing I can do.

00:05:49.077 --> 00:05:50.537
Okay, everybody, listen up!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:51.913
(SHUSHING)

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.373
I gotta send you all home. Right now.

00:05:53.665 --> 00:05:54.624
-Huh?
-What?

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:57.627
Yep. 'Cause like my dad used to say,

00:05:57.711 --> 00:06:00.589
"Get a good night's sleep
and do a great day's work!"

00:06:00.881 --> 00:06:01.923
(GROANS)

00:06:03.508 --> 00:06:07.220
That's right. Rehearsals begin
first thing tomorrow morning.

00:06:07.304 --> 00:06:09.598
And if you wanna become stars
and win 100 grand,

00:06:09.681 --> 00:06:13.268
then you better be ready to work harder than
you've ever worked in your lives.

00:06:13.476 --> 00:06:16.855
So, get some sleep, and dream big dreams!

00:06:17.022 --> 00:06:18.023
(CHEERING)

00:06:18.148 --> 00:06:19.441
JOHNNY: Blimey!
GUNTER: This is great!

00:06:19.941 --> 00:06:21.443
(ALL SINGING)

00:06:21.526 --> 00:06:22.569
Miss Crawly!

00:06:24.654 --> 00:06:27.574
Come on, that's enough now.
Come on, off the stage. Please.

00:06:27.657 --> 00:06:28.742
"Dream big dreams"?

00:06:28.825 --> 00:06:29.826
I know, it's good, right?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:30.952
What about the 100 grand?

00:06:31.077 --> 00:06:33.955
Don't you worry, Eddie.
There's got to be a way to get it.

00:06:34.039 --> 00:06:35.874
What? Buster, no, listen to me!

00:06:36.249 --> 00:06:37.375
This show is not gonna

00:06:37.459 --> 00:06:38.627
save your theater.

00:06:38.752 --> 00:06:40.337
You're at rock bottom, pal.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.465
Yep, and do you know what's great about
hitting rock bottom, Eddie?

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:47.886
There's only one way left to go. And that's up!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:55.060
And you can see the lucky few
leaving the theater behind me.

00:06:55.143 --> 00:06:57.020
-Now back to you in the studio, John...
-(SWITCHES OFF TV)

00:06:57.145 --> 00:06:59.898
-(SNIFFLES)
-Oh, honey, please don't cry.

00:06:59.981 --> 00:07:01.524
You are not a failure.

00:07:01.608 --> 00:07:03.276
There'll be other chances, you just...

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.111
Bah! The heck, there will!

00:07:05.195 --> 00:07:06.446
Dad, please...

00:07:06.529 --> 00:07:08.531
Come on! Don't you want this?

00:07:08.615 --> 00:07:10.283
Well, sure, but I messed it up.

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:12.744
Then you gotta go back
there tomorrow and say,

00:07:12.827 --> 00:07:15.914
"Mr. Moon, I demand you let me re-audition!"

00:07:15.997 --> 00:07:18.541
Be confident! Show 'em
you ain't gonna be pushed around!

00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:21.002
-You got that, Meena?
-Um...

00:07:21.086 --> 00:07:23.463
Good! Now go get my cocoa.

00:07:24.965 --> 00:07:27.842
LANCE: (SINGING) I won't sell out for nobody

00:07:28.385 --> 00:07:30.845
Won't follow no fool

00:07:30.929 --> 00:07:33.598
Would you stop? I'd only be doing it for us.

00:07:33.682 --> 00:07:34.683
(SCOFFS) Oh, really?

00:07:34.766 --> 00:07:37.102
Yes, really! If I won that money,

00:07:37.185 --> 00:07:39.854
we could build our own recording studio,
start our own label.

00:07:39.938 --> 00:07:42.357
I mean, the whole world
would get to hear your songs.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.985
(SINGING) I'm not listening to my girlfriend

00:07:45.068 --> 00:07:46.820
'Cause she just wants to sell out

00:07:46.945 --> 00:07:48.655
(GROANS)

00:07:48.863 --> 00:07:50.865
(PLAYING JAZZ MUSIC)

00:07:56.746 --> 00:07:57.831
Ah...

00:07:58.957 --> 00:08:01.001
(PLAYING ROMANTIC MUSIC)

